@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}
<div class="page-head">
    <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
</div>
<div class="panel" style="max-width: 42rem;">

<p>McWut is a private file drop for people who were invited. It is not a public website, and open registration stays off.</p>

<h2 class="h5">What is stored</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Your email and a hash of your sign-in password.</li>
    <li>Password-vault logins you save. The name is stored as text. The username, password, URL, and notes are encrypted with this site's key. Only you can open your list.</li>
    <li>Files you upload, including the name, type, size, and expiry.</li>
    <li>Text you paste, saved as a text file.</li>
    <li>Share links you create, and a hash of a link password if you set one.</li>
    <li>Short links you create, and the web address they open.</li>
    <li>A short record of uploads, downloads, and deletes.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="h5">Who can see a file</h2>
<ul>
    <li>You, while you are signed in.</li>
    <li>Anyone who has the share link, until it expires or you delete the file. If you set a password, they must enter it first.</li>
    <li>Anyone who has a short link is sent to the web address you saved.</li>
</ul>
<p>Photos can show as thumbnails you can open larger. A short note, including a Markdown file, can be read on My files and on the share page when the link allows preview. Opening that view does not count as a download. SVG and HTML stay downloads.</p>

<h2 class="h5">How long it stays</h2>
<p>You choose 1 day, 7 days, 30 days, or forever. A background cleanup removes expired files from the list and from storage. Turning an account off does not delete that person's files. An admin can turn the account back on. An admin can also set a new sign-in password for a person.</p>

<p class="mb-0">Do not upload anything you are not allowed to keep. Delete a file while you are signed in to remove it. To close an account, ask the admin who invited you.</p>
</div>
